Z||000000||TRiAD||10-27-2001||11:06 AM||||OK, there's this IDIOT on my local forum who used to own a poorly maintained, 4-cylinder Fiero. His was a POS, but it was in terrible shape when he got it, and he didn't do it any favors.<BR>Here's what he posted in reply to my thread "Tell me again what's wrong with Fieros?", complete with the LT1 Chop Top burn-out video attatched...They know I'm buying a GT next weekend...<P><I>"I owned an '87 Fiero (read: DEATHTRAP) for over a year. In short: to this day everytime i see an example of this GM pile of monkey dung chattering, sputtering, and crawling around the roads of our great country, i just shutter and have chills run up my spine and nightmares of massive engine repairs, horrible electronic problems, interior rattles, strange smells, inconvenient everything and horrible suspension running through my brain. I was deluded in my love for the car the way that a mother cares for a horribly deformed retarded child. The way only a crack smoking mother could. <BR>If anyone is offended by my comments i blame Bin laden.<BR>On a pleasent note, the handlling when modified was pretty good. But then that could just be my deluded self talking, back when i was a huge druggie and crack smoker, i think it was ok.<P>P.S. Good friggin luck with that car. Buy an MR2 if you need mid-engine sporty compact. an old Supercharged model would be better than a Fiero no contest. I'd take the 2nd gen turbo anyday, the worst of the 2nd gens would be more reliable then the best of the GM piles that were made hands down."</I><P>Wow...<BR><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
